Start sensors that were claimed while they were still being discovered.

With SSC (libssc) sensors, find_sensors()/driver_open() run synchronous QMI
requests that iterate the main loop, and the bus name is already owned, so a
client (gnome-shell, gsd-power) can call ClaimAccelerometer/ClaimLight before
the device exists. The claim is recorded, but the coldplug path in
name_acquired_handler() never started polling for already-claimed sensors
(the hotplug path in sensor_changes() does), so no orientation or light
reading ever arrived.

--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -777,6 +777,15 @@ name_acquired_handler (GDBusConnection *connection,
 		}
 
 		DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) = sensor_device;
+
+		/* Claimed while we were still discovering it: start it now and
+		 * send the property change with the first measurement, as the
+		 * hotplug path does. */
+		if (g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0) {
+			g_debug ("%s claimed during startup, starting it", driver_type_to_str (i));
+			data->sensor_startup_dbus_event_delayed[i] = TRUE;
+			driver_set_polling (sensor_device, TRUE);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
